            "role": "assistant",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1793211543.794,
          "update_time": 1793211549.04,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Updated the [rewrite note](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/05_radial_theta_collision_geometry/book/changes/02_REWRITE_20261028.md) to make that the organizing priority.\n\nI propose normalizing\n\\[\nF(z)=2\\xi\\!\\left(\\frac{1+iz}{2}\\right)=16H(0,z).\n\\]\nThen the three-dimensional Euclidean formula is\n\\[\n\\boxed{F(z)=(1+z^2)\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\n\\rho_\\Theta(X)e^{izu(X)}\\,dX,}\n\\]\nwhere\n\\[\nu(X)=\\tfrac12\\log|X|,\n\\qquad\n\\rho_\\Theta(X)=\n\\frac{1+|X|^{-1}-\\Theta(|X|)}{16\\pi|X|^{5/2}}.\n\\]\n\nFor the main exposition, the cylinder absorbs those radial weights:\n\\[\n\\boxed{F(z)=(1+z^2)\\int_{\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb S^2}\nG_\\Theta(p)e^{izu(p)}\\,d\\mu(p),}\n\\]\nwith\n\\[\nG_\\Theta(u,\\omega)=\\cosh u-\\tfrac12e^u\\Theta(e^{2u}),\n\\qquad d\\mu=du\\,\\frac{d\\omega}{4\\pi}.\n\\]\n\nThis gives a smooth spatial field and a simple exponential kernel. Both integrals converge for \\(|\\operatorname{Im}z|<1\\); their complete products extend to the entire \\(F\\)."
            ]
          },
